TEXT -192 -56 Left 7 ;Big net\n(Many generators)\n400kV
TEXT 720 -40 Left 7 ;Small net\nOne generator\nat 20kV
TEXT 672 592 Left 6 ;At the start of the simulation there are two seperated nets\nOne net (net1) is very big with a generator(s) having 10000MW nominal power and inertia of J=1e8 (starting at t=2s)\nThe second net (net2) is smaller with a generator of 400MW nominal power and inertia of J=1e5 (start from beginning)\nNet1 has 400kV and Net2 has 20kV nominal voltage\nThe speed of generator 2 is controlled by external PI-controller at startup, whereas the \ngenerator's stator voltage is controlled by external AVR.\nAfter starting gen1 at t=2s the generator is controlled by internal AVR and Speedcontroller\nBetween net1 and net2 there is a ideal Transformer (400kV/20kV) and a switcher\nfor synchronizing the two nets. The switcher is controlled by a very simple synchronizer device\nYou can see that the loadsteps at t=3s and t=7s for gen1 has only small influence at the generator's speed andfrequency of the net1\nbecause the generator nominal power and inertia is very high. On the other side for gen2 here the loadstep of 100MW+20MVAr at t=4s\nlet the freuency and the speed of the generator changing up and down for a short time \nAt 12s the synchronizer is enabled and at 14s net1 and net2 are coupled\nAfter synchronizing the external speed controller of gen2 is disabled and the generator is fed by constant\ntorque corresponding to an active power of 100MW. After short time the active power output of gen2 is increased to 120MW
TEXT 568 304 Left 4 ;Ideal Transformer\n400kV/20kV
